# Button placement and icons

## Default class (hard rule)

- Whenever the user asks to create a button, use `className="btn-primary px-3 sm:px-4"` unless they explicitly request a different style (`outline`, `delete-btn`, ghost, text link, etc.).
- `.btn-primary` and `.primary-btn` are aliases (same styles). Prefer `btn-primary` for new buttons.
- Do **not** default to `variant="outline"`, plain `Button`, or unstyled links when the user just says “add a button.”

```tsx
{/* Default when the user says "add a button" */}
<Button className="btn-primary px-3 sm:px-4">
  <Plus className="h-4 w-4" />
  Add
</Button>
```

## Placement (hard rule)

- Put action buttons on the **right** of their row, toolbar, form footer, or card action strip.
- Use `flex … justify-end` (or `ml-auto` on the button group when the row mixes left content with right actions).
- Do **not** leave primary actions flush-left unless the user explicitly asks for left placement.
- Tab/segment controls that sit with a separate action (e.g. Refresh) still keep the whole control group right-aligned, or put tabs left and actions right with `justify-between` — never leave a lone primary CTA on the left.

```tsx
{/* Page / section actions */}
<div className="mb-6 flex items-center justify-end gap-3">
  <Button className="btn-primary px-3 sm:px-4">
    <Plus className="h-4 w-4" />
    Add
  </Button>
</div>

{/* Form submit under fields */}
<div className="flex justify-end">
  <Button className="btn-primary px-3 sm:px-4">
    <Plus className="h-4 w-4" />
    Save
  </Button>
</div>
```

## Icons (hard rule)

- Every `btn-primary` / `primary-btn` button must include a Lucide icon (`h-4 w-4`) plus a label — never text-only.
- Prefer the same for outline action buttons in funding/forms toolbars (Refresh, Convert, etc.).
- Icon before label; match existing CAALM patterns (`Plus`, `Check`, `Trash2`, `RefreshCw`, etc.).

## Exceptions

- Only deviate from `btn-primary` when the user explicitly requests a different style, position, or an icon-only control.
- Destructive confirms use `.delete-btn` (see dialog rules).
- Row overflow menus stay as documented in `global-style-guide.mdc` (dots.svg), not this rule.
